The exterior angles sum to $360^{\circ}$.
$$\begin{align*}
\text{Missing exterior angle} &= 360^{\circ}-(52^{\circ}+82^{\circ}+81^{\circ}+86^{\circ})\\
&=59^{\circ}
\end{align*}$$
The interior angle and its exterior angle are supplementary.
$$\begin{align*}
3x+16+59 &=180\\
3x &=105\\
x &=35^{\circ}
\end{align*}$$
